# What the build context of `plateforme/Dockerfile` MUST NOT
# carry.
#
# 🔴 IT IS NAMED AFTER ITS DOCKERFILE, AND IT IS DELIBERATE. BuildKit reads
# `<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore` in priority over the `.dockerignore` at
# the root of the context. Placing a `.dockerignore` AT THE ROOT would ALSO have bounded
# the build of `./Dockerfile`, the image of the historical Guacamole, which
# does not belong to sub-project ⑤ — a shared file whose meaning is changed
# without saying so is the failure mode this repository pays for most often.
#
# The context is the root of the repository because three production files
# import `proto/ts/`; see the box at the head of `plateforme/Dockerfile`.

# Everything is excluded, then exactly what the image copies is reopened.
*

!plateforme/package.json
!plateforme/package-lock.json
!plateforme/tsconfig.json
!plateforme/src
!proto/ts

# ⚠️ RE-EXCLUSIONS, AFTER the negations: a negation cannot reopen what
# a LATER rule closes again, and that is what actually bounds the size
# of the context.
plateforme/node_modules
proto/ts/**/*.test.ts
